title: 'Founder test round 1: voice regression found, Settings + theme switch built, clickable options + single spoken marker built'
summary: |-
  The founder's live test of 3b5c7139 surfaced several issues.
  - (1) A voice speaker-verification regression: the enrolled founder was rejected as unknown, and after re-enrol a nearby VIDEO was accepted as "matt". Turns lag ~60 s and all carry an identical textHash. Verification worked at 07:14Z on the old build. I ruled out decodeAsync mutating samples (identical embeddings before and after). A debugging builder is reproducing with real models and bisecting. I advised the founder to turn ambient off meanwhile.
  - (2) No visible light mode or settings: theme lived only in ⌘K and memory. Built (19716538/374403c2/58d0f241):
    - a header ☀Day/☾Night/◐Auto switch, persisted per browser;
    - a Settings sheet (⚙, ⌘,) covering Appearance/Layout/Voice/Permissions/About, every control an existing command or read-only with a how-to.
    It also fixed the standing feed's inline styles, which the CSP had silently blocked.
  - (3) Lettered options as clickable chips (895193b2): they send exactly the shown text via the composer path and are dashed, never key-styled.
  - (4) Pipelined TTS produced N "spoken aloud" rows per reply; now one marker per reply, with duration and · stopped (c54144af).
  - (5) A model picker plus a resume-preserving switch is in progress.
  - (6) Context meter designed (see previous lore).
  Aegis reviews launched for (2) and (3).
